            "type": "dita",
            "id": "4f1c7a92b3d85e02",
            "text": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n<concept id=\"tmdm-roles-and-projected-edges\" xml:lang=\"en\">\n  <title>TMDM Roles and Projected Edges</title>\n  <shortdesc>A TMDM Association has Roles, and each Role has a type and a player. The Topicmap draws one edge for each Role; the edge is an object of the HyperDoc projection and the direction it is drawn in comes from the projection, not from the Role.</shortdesc>\n  <conbody>\n    <section>\n      <title>Six things around one Role</title>\n      <p>The example is the Role <codeph>action</codeph> of the Association <codeph>proposes</codeph> in the Topicmap of the edit proposal for the Item E3 (see <xref href=\"hyperdoc:item:4f1c7a92b3d85e01\" scope=\"local\" format=\"dita\">Topicmap Signs and Represented Objects</xref>).</p>\n      <dl>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>TMDM Association</dt>\n          <dd><xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:proposes-association\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">proposes</xref>: a statement with a type, a Scope and a set of Roles. It has no first or second Role.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>TMDM Association Role</dt>\n          <dd><xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:proposes-role-action\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">The Role action of proposes</xref>, an <xref href=\"hyperdoc:class:topic-maps.tmdm:association-role\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">association-role</xref>. It has a parent Association, a type and a player, and nothing else.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>Role Type</dt>\n          <dd><xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:role-type-action\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">The Topic action</xref>, a TMDM Topic that names what the player is in this Association.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>Role Player</dt>\n          <dd><xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:player-the-proposed-action\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">The Topic the-proposed-action</xref>, the TMDM Topic that plays the Role. Its projected Topic is <xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:player-topic-the-proposed-action\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">the-proposed-action</xref> and the Lisp object it was made from is <xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:the-proposed-action-object\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">the proposed Action</xref>.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>projected-tmdm-association</dt>\n          <dd><xref href=\"hyperdoc:example:proposes-edge-action\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">The HyperDoc object for the Role</xref>, an object of the class <xref href=\"hyperdoc:class:dreyeck/topic-maps-reading:projected-tmdm-association\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">projected-tmdm-association</xref>, which is a topicmap-association of the projection. Its id is <codeph>proposes(action=the-proposed-action,proposal=the-proposal):action:the-proposed-action</codeph>; its type is the Role type <codeph>action</codeph>; its <codeph>from</codeph> is the id of the Association node and its <codeph>to</codeph> is the id of the player. Its properties hold the TMDM Role (<codeph>:tmdm-role</codeph>), the Role type, the TMDM Association and the Association type. Where the projection stands for a Role, that is the object the edge represents.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n        <dlentry>\n          <dt>SVG edge</dt>\n          <dd>The element a renderer draws for the projected-tmdm-association. The native renderer draws a line, and over it a transparent wider hit line of class <codeph>dreyeck-topicmap-association-hit</codeph>; the hit line takes the gesture. TALA (interactive) draws the group of the edge, with the attribute <codeph>data-association-id</codeph>, and that group takes the gesture. Neither element is the Role; each is bound to the projected-tmdm-association that stands for it.</dd>\n        </dlentry>\n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>The direction of an edge</title>\n      <p>For every Role of an Association node the projection sets <codeph>from</codeph> to the node and <codeph>to</codeph> to the player, whatever the Role type is. The two edges of <codeph>proposes</codeph> therefore both leave the node, one to the proposal and one to the Action, although the Roles are of two different types. The native renderer puts an arrowhead at the end of the player. The way an edge is drawn tells which Association node and which player it joins. It states nothing about the Role: a TMDM Role has a type and a player and no direction, and no reading of the drawing may infer that the player acts on, or is acted on by, the Association. The Role type that is written on the edge is what says what the player is.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>Reaching the objects</title>\n      <p>Inspect represented object on the edge opens the TMDM Role. From the Role, the Slots view links its parent Association, its type and its player, so that the Association, the Role type and the player are reachable from the edge. Inspect represented object on the Association node opens the TMDM Association instead; Inspect Topicmap sign on the node opens the projected Topic. How to press is in <xref href=\"hyperdoc:item:4f1c7a92b3d85e04\" scope=\"local\" format=\"dita\">Inspect a Topicmap Sign</xref>.</p>\n    </section>\n  </conbody>\n</concept>\n",
            "ditaVersion": "1.3",
            "infoType": "concept"
          },
          {
            "type": "dita",
            "id": "4f1c7a92b3d85e03",
            "text": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n<reference id=\"topicmap-gesture-operations\" xml:lang=\"en\">\n  <title>Topicmap Gesture Operations</title>\n  <shortdesc>The read-only Operations that a secondary press on a Topicmap sign offers: Inspect Topicmap sign, Inspect represented object and Inspect relation contract. For each: its identity, its Bindings, its target, where it applies, the sector it is chosen in, and the object it returns.</shortdesc>\n  <refbody>\n    <section>\n      <title>Scope of this list</title>\n      <p>The list is read from the source code of <filepath>dreyeck/src/topicmap-gesture.lisp</filepath> and <filepath>dreyeck/src/gesture-binding-witness.lisp</filepath>: the Bindings <xref href=\"hyperdoc:variable:dreyeck/inspector/topicmap:*workspace-action-sign-bindings*\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">workspace-action-sign-bindings</xref> of a Topic sign, <xref href=\"hyperdoc:variable:dreyeck/inspector/topicmap:*association-role-bindings*\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">association-role-bindings</xref> of the sign of a TMDM Role, and the Bindings of <xref href=\"hyperdoc:function:dreyeck/gesture-binding-witness:make-association-binding-catalog\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">make-association-binding-catalog</xref>. Other systems add Operations for the Topics of their own domain through a method on <codeph>workspace-action-sign-bindings</codeph>; those are not listed here, and this list makes no claim about the Operations of other HyperDoc domains. A Binding comes in two kinds with one Operation: the radial menu, which a press-and-wait reveals after 500 ms, and the learned mark, a direction move made at once.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>Inspect Topicmap sign</title>\n      <simpletable><sthead><stentry>Property</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry><stentry>Notes</stentry></sthead>\n        <strow><stentry>Operation identity</stentry><stentry><xref href=\"hyperdoc:operation:inspect-topicmap-sign\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\"><codeph>operation/inspect-topicmap-sign</codeph></xref></stentry><stentry>Title: Inspect Topicmap sign. Data only: it names what is asked and holds no executor.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Bindings</stentry><stentry><codeph>binding/radial-menu-inspect-topicmap-sign</codeph>, <codeph>binding/learned-mark-inspect-topicmap-sign</codeph></stentry><stentry>One for the menu and one for the mark, in the same sector.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Gesture target</stentry><stentry><codeph>:workspace-action-sign-occurrence</codeph></stentry><stentry>The occurrence of a Topic sign: its Topic, projection and Workspace.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Applies to</stentry><stentry>The sign of a Topic</stentry><stentry>The native workspace action sign of a Topic and the Topic group of TALA (interactive). Not the sign of an Association.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Sector</stentry><stentry>center 270 degrees (up), half width 30 degrees</stentry><stentry>Degrees are measured so that 0 is to the right, 180 to the left and 270 up.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Returns</stentry><stentry>The projected Topic of the occurrence</stentry><stentry>A topicmap-topic of the projection; for the Topicmap of an Item edit an item-edit-topic. It is the object that PRIMARY opens on a TALA Topic group.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Not applicable when</stentry><stentry>The target carries no Topic sign occurrence</stentry><stentry>The Operation signals operation-not-applicable; nothing opens.</stentry></strow>\n      </simpletable>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>Inspect represented object</title>\n      <simpletable><sthead><stentry>Property</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry><stentry>Notes</stentry></sthead>\n        <strow><stentry>Operation identity</stentry><stentry><xref href=\"hyperdoc:operation:inspect-represented-object\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\"><codeph>operation/inspect-represented-object</codeph></xref></stentry><stentry>Title: Inspect represented object.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Bindings on a Topic sign</stentry><stentry><codeph>binding/radial-menu-inspect-represented-object</codeph>, <codeph>binding/learned-mark-inspect-represented-object</codeph></stentry><stentry>Target type :workspace-action-sign-occurrence. Omitted for an occurrence whose Topic has no represented object.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Bindings on a Role sign</stentry><stentry><codeph>binding/radial-menu-association-inspect-represented-object</codeph>, <codeph>binding/learned-mark-association-inspect-represented-object</codeph></stentry><stentry>Target type :topicmap-association. Offered only for an Association that stands for a TMDM Role, one that has the property :tmdm-role.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Gesture target</stentry><stentry><codeph>:workspace-action-sign-occurrence</codeph> or <codeph>:topicmap-association</codeph></stentry><stentry>For an Association the target carries the exact Association object under :association; an id or a label names none.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Applies to</stentry><stentry>The sign of a Topic that has a represented object; the edge of a TMDM Role</stentry><stentry>The native Role edge (its hit line) and the Association edge of TALA (interactive).</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Sector</stentry><stentry>center 180 degrees (left), half width 30 degrees</stentry><stentry>The same sector on a Topic sign and on a Role edge.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Returns</stentry><stentry>On a Topic sign, the object the Topic represents; on a Role edge, the TMDM Role</stentry><stentry>For a Topic sign it is the value of topicmap-topic-object-of: a TMDM Topic or a TMDM Association. For a Role edge it is the association-role itself, not the Association, the Role type or the player.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Not applicable when</stentry><stentry>The Topic has no represented object; the Association stands for no TMDM Role</stentry><stentry>The Operation signals operation-not-applicable and nothing opens.</stentry></strow>\n      </simpletable>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>Inspect relation contract</title>\n      <simpletable><sthead><stentry>Property</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry><stentry>Notes</stentry></sthead>\n        <strow><stentry>Operation identity</stentry><stentry><xref href=\"hyperdoc:operation:inspect-relation-contract\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\"><codeph>operation/inspect-relation-contract</codeph></xref></stentry><stentry>Title: Inspect relation contract.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Bindings</stentry><stentry><codeph>binding/radial-inspect-relation-contract</codeph>, <codeph>binding/mark-inspect-relation-contract</codeph></stentry><stentry>Target type :topicmap-association.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Gesture target</stentry><stentry><codeph>:topicmap-association</codeph></stentry><stentry>The exact Association.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Applies to</stentry><stentry>An Association that has a Relation Contract</stentry><stentry>It is offered when the Association has the property :relation-contract, as the Work relations of a Work Topicmap do. A TMDM Role edge of an Item edit has none, so it never offers this Operation.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Sector</stentry><stentry>center 0 degrees (right), half width 30 degrees</stentry><stentry>Not the sector of Inspect represented object, so that an Association that has both offers two distinct directions.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Returns</stentry><stentry>The Relation Contract Topic of the Association</stentry><stentry>The Topic that the :relation-contract property holds.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Not applicable when</stentry><stentry>The Association refers to no Relation Contract</stentry><stentry>The Operation signals operation-not-applicable and nothing opens.</stentry></strow>\n      </simpletable>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>PRIMARY and SECONDARY on each surface</title>\n      <simpletable>\n        <sthead><stentry>Surface</stentry><stentry>PRIMARY click</stentry><stentry>SECONDARY offers</stentry><stentry>Point and History</stentry></sthead>\n        <strow><stentry>Native Topicmap, Topic sign</stentry><stentry>Moves the Workspace Point to the Topic (topicmap-workspace-go-to).</stentry><stentry>Inspect Topicmap sign and, if there is a represented object, Inspect represented object.</stentry><stentry>PRIMARY moves the Point and records the Point it left in the History. SECONDARY changes neither.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Native Topicmap, edge of a TMDM Role</stentry><stentry>Nothing: no pane opens and the Point stays.</stentry><stentry>Inspect represented object only.</stentry><stentry>Neither changes the Point or the History.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>Native Topicmap, edge of a Work relation</stentry><stentry>Nothing: the drawn edge has neither an Inspector reference nor a gesture.</stentry><stentry>Nothing: this edge takes no gesture.</stentry><stentry>Not applicable.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>TALA (interactive), Topic group</stentry><stentry>Opens the projected Topic as an Inspector object.</stentry><stentry>The same two Operations as the native sign. There is no Workspace here.</stentry><stentry>There is no Workspace in this drawing, so neither click touches a Point or a History.</stentry></strow>\n        <strow><stentry>TALA (interactive), Association group</stentry><stentry>Opens the Association (a projected-tmdm-association for a Role) as an Inspector object.</stentry><stentry>Inspect relation contract if the Association has a Relation Contract; Inspect represented object if it stands for a TMDM Role; nothing if it has neither.</stentry><stentry>No Workspace here either.</stentry></strow>\n      </simpletable>\n    </section>\n    <section>\n      <title>Where the claims come from</title>\n      <ul>\n        <li>The sectors, Binding ids and target types are the values of the three Binding catalogues named above; the tests of this documentation compare this topic with them.</li>\n        <li>The returned objects are the methods of <xref href=\"hyperdoc:function:dreyeck/inspector/topicmap:operation-inspectable-object\" scope=\"external\" format=\"hyperdoc\">operation-inspectable-object</xref> for the Operation and the target.</li>\n        <li>The surfaces are the renderer <filepath>dreyeck/src/topicmap-inspector.lisp</filepath> (the native Topicmap), <filepath>dreyeck/src/topicmap-tala-inspector.lisp</filepath> (TALA (interactive)) and the binder in <filepath>dreyeck/src/topicmap-gesture.lisp</filepath>.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n  </refbody>\n</reference>\n",
